NEARS-2428 QA finding — success branch Log::info() line is below the deployed
LOG_LEVEL threshold and never reaches laravel.log in the project's standard
config, breaking AC2 ("On successful send, laravel.log gains a new log line
recording the send").

## Fix under test (Admin/app/Traits/NotificationTrait.php, diff vs dd9a2a2c)
    if ($response->successful()) {
        \Log::info('FCM notification sent', [
            'status' => $response->status(),
        ]);
        return true;
    }
    // ...
    \Log::error('FCM notification send failed', [...]);

## Project-standard config (both are LOG_LEVEL=warning — not a worktree quirk)
$ grep -n "LOG_LEVEL" Admin/.env.example
18:LOG_LEVEL=warning
$ grep -n "LOG_LEVEL" /Users/Apple/Projects/nears/Admin/.env   # primary tree, same value
16:LOG_LEVEL=warning

## config/logging.php — 'single' channel (backs laravel.log via SizeCappedFileHandler)
        'single' => [
            'driver' => 'monolog',
            'handler' => \App\Logging\SizeCappedFileHandler::class,
            'handler_with' => [
                'path' => storage_path('logs/laravel.log'),
                'maxBytes' => \App\Logging\SizeCappedFileHandler::DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES,
            ],
            'level' => env('LOG_LEVEL', 'debug'),
        ],
=> channel minimum level = env('LOG_LEVEL') = 'warning'. Monolog's severity
order is DEBUG < INFO < NOTICE < WARNING < ERROR — an INFO-level record is
BELOW 'warning' and Monolog drops it before it ever reaches the handler.
ERROR-level records (the failure/exception branches) are ABOVE 'warning' and
are written normally — this is exactly why AC3's failure line appears live
below but AC2's success line would not, under the same deployed config.

## Live probe (php artisan tinker, worktree Admin/, run 2026-08-24 04:55:54)
Command:
    \Log::info('NEARS-2428 QA probe: FCM notification sent', ['status' => 200]);
    \Log::error('NEARS-2428 QA probe: FCM notification send failed', ['status' => 404, 'reason' => 'Not Found']);

Result — grep of storage/logs/laravel.log immediately after:
    $ grep -F "NEARS-2428 QA probe" storage/logs/laravel.log
    [2026-08-24 04:55:54] production.ERROR: NEARS-2428 QA probe: FCM notification send failed {"status":404,"reason":"Not Found"}

The paired \Log::info(...) probe line (identical severity/shape to the fix's
success-branch call) does NOT appear anywhere in the file — it was silently
dropped by the 'warning' floor. Only the \Log::error(...) probe line landed.

## Conclusion
Under the project's own default/standard .env (LOG_LEVEL=warning, matching
both .env.example and the primary tree's live .env), a successful FCM send
through the newly-fixed sendNotificationToHttp() will return true (AC1 holds)
but will NOT produce any new line in laravel.log (AC2 does not hold) — the
exact silent-logging symptom this ticket exists to fix survives on the
success path specifically, because \Log::info() is the wrong severity for
this deployment's log floor. \Log::error()/\Log::warning() would both clear
the floor; \Log::info() does not.

filed as: task_bug (breaks_ac: true, AC2) against Admin/app/Traits/NotificationTrait.php
